    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0561" n="487" xml:id="pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1322</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Russia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-23T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Your 15 [13], March 16,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d460-f1"/> and 17, March
                        18.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d460-f2"/> Department believes your action has had
                    good effect, but does not desire to modify in any way previous instructions as
                    to recognition of Soviet government. As conditions change so rapidly Department
                    has issued you only general instructions and relies on your discretion and
                    judgment to determine your movements and matters not affecting policy of this
                    Government. Unhappily, the United States is unable to extend direct aid to the
                    people of Russia at this time but desires you to reflect attitude of America as
                    already conveyed to you in previous telegrams.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d460-f1" n="1" xml:id="d460-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; discusses, as does No. 17, the Ambassador’s press declaration
                    opposing a separate peace.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d460-f2" n="2" xml:id="d460-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg402">p. 402</ref>.</p>
